    "result": "I implemented `invoice_totals` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`, and wrote 31 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`. `python -m pytest -q tests` now passes (31 passed). One test failed on the first run because I had written its input wrong (unit price 100 instead of 10), so I corrected the test and kept the code unchanged. I have not run the coverage, CRAP, mutation or bandit gates, since only the test command is allowed. The tests were written to exercise every branch, but the mutation score is unverified. The code uses `ROUND_HALF_UP` per line, applies the bulk discount multiplicatively for standard lines at qty 10 or more, and raises `ValueError` for all the invalid inputs listed in the spec. The tests cover the rounding edge cases, the qty and discount boundaries, credit handling, and `tax_by_rate` with and without zero rates.",
